---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout>

  <section class="hero">

    <img
      src="/SVG-DBR-LOGO.png"
      alt="Dual Brain Robotics Logo"
      class="hero-logo"
    />

    <h1>Dual Brain Robotics</h1>

    <h2>
      A Bilateral Cognitive Architecture for Advanced Robotics
    </h2>

    <p>
      Developed by Dr. Alexander Durig, Dual Brain Robotics explores a
      new approach to artificial intelligence and robotics inspired by
      the cooperative structure of the human brain.
    </p>

    <p>
      A U.S. Utility-Provisional Patent Application has been filed for
      the Dual Brain Robotics Architecture.
    </p>

    <div class="patent-status">
      U.S. Utility-Provisional Patent Application<br />
      Dual Brain Robotics Architecture<br />
      Application No. 64/181,346
    </div>

    <a href="/architecture" class="button">
      Explore the Architecture
    </a>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>The Robotics Challenge</h2>

    <p>
      Modern robots can perform highly precise tasks in structured
      environments, yet many still struggle with smooth movement,
      dexterity, balance, adaptive behavior, and micro-coordination.
    </p>

    <p>
      Walking across uneven terrain, manipulating delicate objects,
      and responding gracefully to unexpected changes remain difficult
      challenges for many robotic systems.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>The Proposed Solution</h2>

    <p>
      Dual Brain Robotics investigates whether robotic capability can
      be enhanced through the interaction of two complementary
      cognitive systems rather than a single centralized pathway.
    </p>

    <p>
      The architecture proposes bilateral perception, reciprocal
      monitoring, coordinated prediction, and integrated motor
      decision making inspired by biological cognition.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Two Minds. One Intelligence.</h2>

    <p>
      Rather than concentrating all processing within a single
      decision engine, Dual Brain Robotics explores the possibility
      that intelligence may emerge from cooperation between
      complementary cognitive systems.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Potential Advantages</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Smoother robotic movement</li>
      <li>Improved dexterity</li>
      <li>Bilateral error correction</li>
      <li>Micro-coordination</li>
      <li>Adaptive behavior</li>
      <li>Enhanced environmental awareness</li>
      <li>Improved human-robot interaction</li>
    </ul>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Research Foundation</h2>

    <p>
      The architecture draws upon decades of work in social
      psychology, perception theory, autism research,
      consciousness studies, and cognitive modeling.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>The Beginning of a New Exploration</h2>

    <p>
      Dual Brain Robotics represents an effort to unite artificial
      intelligence, robotics, perception theory, and consciousness
       prototyping are
      currently underway.
    </p>

  </section>

</MainLayout>
